REM Protects the word `label` used as a name: a label declaration alone on a line, a
REM declaration immediately followed by a statement (with and without a space, including a
REM semicolon-chained pair and an ENTER statement), a GOTO/GOSUB and multi-target ON...GOTO
REM branch target, including inside a semicolon-chained statement, and a plain variable
REM written and read inside an expression -- in upper, lower and mixed case, alongside an
REM ordinary non-keyword label declaration in front of a statement for the general case.
LET X=0
GOSUB label
goto Label
LET X=0;GOTO LABEL
ON X GOTO label,other
LABEL=5
Y=LABEL+1
GOTO after
label:
RETURN
LABEL:ESCAPE
Label: escape;exit
LABEL: ENTER A$,B$
other:Z=1
RETURN
after:W=1
